# FloRun deployment configuration.
#
# You usually do NOT need to copy this file: `deploy/install.sh` asks for these
# values on a first install and writes config.florun for you (and
# `--reconfigure` re-runs those questions later). This file is the annotated
# reference for what each value means -- and the manual path, if you would
# rather write the config yourself:
#
#   cp config.florun.example config.florun     # from inside the checkout
#
# An existing config.florun is never overwritten by the installer; it is read
# and validated instead.
#
# config.florun lives INSIDE the checkout and is gitignored, so a pull can
# never overwrite it and nothing is written outside this directory. It holds NO
# secrets -- the Cloudflare tunnel token is kept in a podman secret.
#
# Format: plain KEY=value, no spaces around `=`, no quotes. The updater parses
# this file as DATA (it is never executed), validates every value against the
# character sets noted below, and aborts loudly -- with the running site
# untouched -- on anything suspicious.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HOSTING THIS YOURSELF (fresh server bootstrap)
#   1. git clone https://github.com/jordanp123/florun.git ~/florun
#   2. cd ~/florun && ./deploy/install.sh
#
#   The installer asks for the values below, offers to store the Cloudflare
#   tunnel token as a podman secret, and prints whatever is left to do. Make
#   the tunnel in the Cloudflare Zero Trust dashboard first and route your
#   hostname to  http://website:8080
#
#   Everything -- config, logs, the build context -- stays inside ~/florun.
#   Nothing is written to your home directory or anywhere else.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Unprivileged UIDs the containers run as. Pick a range unused by other stacks
# on the same host -- distinct per-app UIDs mean one compromised container
# cannot touch another app's processes. The two MUST differ from each other,
# and both must be BELOW the UserNS size in the quadlet units (65536), or the
# container has nowhere to map and will not start; install.sh refuses rather
# than let that fail later.
APP_UID=17011
TUNNEL_UID=17010

# Container-name prefix (must be unique per stack on the host).
# Letters/digits/_- only.
STACK_NAME=FloRun

# URL path segment the site is served under: https://your.domain/<SUBPATH>/
# Letters/digits/._- only. A single dot (SUBPATH=.) serves at the domain root,
# which is the stock FloRun setup -- it expects its own subdomain, e.g.
# florun.example.com, so the service worker controls the whole origin and the
# manifest start_url is simply "/".
#
# If you DO serve from a subpath, point the Cloudflare tunnel route at the
# matching hostname/path; the app itself uses relative URLs throughout and
# needs no other change.
SUBPATH=.

# There is deliberately no REPO_URL or CHECKOUT_DIR. Both only ever mattered
# for cloning the repo on a fresh server, and by the time anything reads this
# file the clone has already happened -- the updater pulls from whatever remote
# the checkout has. Config that is never read is config that eventually lies.
